Summary:
During today’s session, the focus was on revising core concepts of Express.js to strengthen backend development understanding. Key topics such as routing, middleware, request and response handling, and API structure were reviewed. Practical examples were considered to understand how Express manages server-side logic and handles client requests. This revision helped in reinforcing the fundamentals required for building efficient backend services.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, there was a clearer understanding of how Express.js works in handling web applications and APIs. The revision improved confidence in structuring routes and using middleware effectively. It also enhanced the ability to manage server-side operations and handle different types of requests. Overall, the session strengthened backend development skills using Express.js.
